# evidence-for: FR-003, FR-004, AC-006
#
# D-012 changed what the per-anchor digest is taken over: the cited line is now decoded
# with surrogateescape and re-encoded with it, instead of being decoded with
# errors="replace", which collapsed every undecodable byte to one U+FFFD and let a
# latin-1 cited line change under a matching hash. For a file that is valid UTF-8 the
# two decodes are identical and there are no surrogates to re-encode, so every digest
# recorded before the fix still matches and no committed manifest is re-reported as
# drift. This records that end to end: the fixture tree is recorded by drift.py as it
# stood at 19c97f9, checked by drift.py at HEAD, and then re-recorded at HEAD, and the
# two manifests are compared byte for byte.

